In article <2086@isgtec.UUCP>, ken@isgtec.uucp (Ken Newman) writes...

>A simple question - is there any way to have your cat/dog NOT attack
>peaceful creatures? He seems to attack just about anything. Last game
>my cat started chewing on some hobbits, so they killed him. I'm assuming
>peaceful creatures really have uses, and it is worthwhile not to just
>pound them.

>- kn


========

	Besides leading them away, there really isn't a way.  You can usually 
lead your pet into a corridor and then circle around and block it off.  But, 
your second assumption, that peaceful creatures have uses is pretty much false.  
They are just NOT enemies.  Ignore them, or try to kill them (although attacking 
certain friendlies does do bad things for luck, I believe, (unicorns and 
shopkeepers spring to mind).  And chaotics can get away w/ that, I think.  
	Again, the simplest way is either get a TOUGH pet, who won't get killed, 
or leash it, and drag it away.

